# EDITED INTENTIONALLY -- this overrides the file {targets} generates.
#
# {targets} writes a version of this file that ignores everything except
# meta/meta. We deliberately also commit objects/ so that a fresh clone of this
# repo is already up to date, matching 01_gfw_data_pull and 03_quarto_notebook.
#
# This pipeline is the one most worth committing. Re-running it needs a
# Copernicus Atmosphere Data Store token that most users will not have, and
# pulls ~6 GB of transient CAMS downloads. Committing the store is what lets
# everyone else treat its outputs as given rather than re-deriving them.
# See README, "Working across machines".
#
# The objects are small -- ~30 KB for the whole pipeline. Most of this
# pipeline's targets are format = "file", which record only a path and hash and
# store nothing here.
#
# Consequences to be aware of:
#   - Object files are binary and re-commit in full whenever data changes.
#     Keep an eye on repo size; run `git gc` periodically.
#   - Only run the pipeline on one machine at a time, and always pull first.
#     Two machines running it independently will conflict on meta/meta.
#   - meta/process (pid, timestamps) and meta/progress (per-run status) stay
#     ignored: they change on every run and carry no reproducibility value.
*
!.gitignore
!meta
meta/*
!meta/meta
!objects
!objects/*
